  "id": "COMPOUND:27848 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (1R,2R,4S,5S,6R,7S)-4,5-Epoxygermacra-9Z-En-1,2,6-Triol and Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, mediated through the target receptor Taste receptor type 2 member 31. This compound is identified as a target of two different molecules, 8,19-Dihydroxyserrulat-14-Ene and Leoheterin, both of which are linked to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The shared target of these two molecules, along with the presence of a common target in the pathway, indicates a possible mechanism of action where the compound may influence the activity of the enzyme through its interaction with the receptor. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the receptor, which in turn affects the enzyme's function, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
